body:
This one is "interesting" - what is going on here is that SystemJS builder is auto-detecting https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/master/modules/angular2/src/router/route_definition.ts as a file with "global module" system. This happens since https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/master/modules/angular2/src/router/route_definition.ts is "empty" - that is - it contains only TS interface definitions so after transpilation to JS it is effectively empty.

I guess this started to be a problem after TS or SystemJS version update, since the "empty" file was there from like 2.0.0-alpha.32 (4d28167bc075a57fd204d23abbf4e408b78a406c).

@hitmanmcc as a work-arround you can add "global" plugin to your SystemJS config.
@btford I guess this should have med / high priority as I guess it will break people's code quite often...
